  "grid_other": "Reminder when a belt test is due",
  "speak1": "Knowing who paid without opening WhatsApp.\n\"If I could see one red list of who owes me, I would sleep.\"",
  "speak2": "Last Ramadan: 30 kids paused, nobody wrote it down.\nAfter Eid he charged 6 families who had paused — they were angry,\none family left. He paid back by hand.",
  "speak3": "Parents: \"why did I get the reminder, I paid\".\n\"When is my son’s belt test?\" — asked again and again.",
  "speak4": "Parent opens the app, sees: paid ✓, next class, belt, attendance.\nHe only gets a message when something needs HIM.",
  "speak5": "Ask about the coaches’ pay — calculating per class at month end\ntakes him a full evening.",
  "free": "— Lost about 1 in 10 kids last year \"quietly\" — no follow-up.\n— Will NOT use anything that sends parents messages he can’t control.\n— Sibling discount is done in his head — every month a different number.\n— Wants the coach to mark attendance on the tablet at the door.\n— Federation entry list took 2 evenings in Excel.\n— Would pay yearly if the first month proves it works.\n«أبي شي بسيط، الوالدين ما يبون تطبيق معقد»\n— Likes that Arabic + English sit side by side.\n— Asked if he can import his Excel list — 140 names.",
  "sum_pains": "1. Chasing payments (2–3 h / week, never sure who paid)\n2. Pauses / freezes not recorded → wrong charges\n3. Attendance on paper → kids drop out unnoticed",
  "sum_quote": "\"If I could see one red list of who owes me, I would sleep.\"",
  "sum_missing": "Freeze / pause · sibling discount · coach pay per class ·\nbelt-test reminders",
  "sum_next": "Show him a demo with his own Excel list — week of 10 Nov",
